---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Strudel from '../components/Strudel.astro';
import { CHAPTERS, SITE_TITLE, withBase } from '../consts';

const demo = `// press the play button, then edit and press ctrl+enter
setcpm(120/4)

$: s("bd*4").bank("RolandTR909").duckorbit(2).duckattack(0.25).duckdepth(0.9)

$: n("0 [~ 3] 5 [7 ~]").scale("C2:minor")
  .s("sawtooth").lpf(sine.range(300, 1600).slow(8)).lpq(6)
  .room(0.4).orbit(2)

$: s("hh*8").gain("[.3 .7]*4").pan(sine.fast(2)).orbit(3)`;
---

<Base title="Home">
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Interactive</p>
    <h1>{SITE_TITLE}</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Strudel is live-codeable music in the browser. This is a guided track through its syntax and —
      more importantly — what its functions actually <em>do</em>: filters, LFOs, envelopes, orbits
      and ducking. Every code block on this site is a real, editable, playable Strudel REPL.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Strudel code={demo} label="taste test — a kick ducking a bassline" />

  <p>
    That patch already uses most of what this site teaches: mini-notation rhythm, a scale, a
    resonant lowpass swept by a signal, separate <strong>orbits</strong> for bass and hats, and a
    kick <strong>ducking</strong> the bass orbit. By the end you will be able to write it from
    scratch and know why every line is there.
  </p>

  <h2>How to use this</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Click into any code box and press <code>ctrl+enter</code></strong> to play it,{' '}
      <code>ctrl+.</code> to stop. Editing is the point — change a number, re-evaluate, listen.
    </li>
    <li>
      Only one box plays at a time. Starting a new one stops the previous.
    </li>
    <li>
      Chapters build on each other. Skipping ahead to{' '}
      <a href={withBase('/tutorial/ducking')}>Ducking</a> works, but it assumes{' '}
      <a href={withBase('/tutorial/orbits')}>Orbits</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Sounds load lazily. The first time you trigger a new sample there may be a short silence.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The track</h2>
  <div class="progress-panel" data-progress-ui hidden>
    <div><span class="count" data-progress-count>0 / 0</span> chapters done</div>
    <div class="progress-bar" aria-hidden="true">
      <span data-progress-fill></span>
    </div>
    <a
      class="progress-continue"
      data-progress-continue
      href={withBase(`/tutorial/${CHAPTERS[0].slug}`)}
      hidden
    >
      <span data-progress-continue-label>Start with</span>{' '}
      <span data-progress-continue-title>{CHAPTERS[0].title}</span> →
    </a>
    <div class="progress-alldone" data-progress-alldone hidden>✓ every chapter done</div>
    <button type="button" class="progress-reset" data-progress-reset>Reset progress</button>
  </div>
  <div class="card-grid">
    {
      CHAPTERS.map((chapter, i) => (
        <a class="card" href={withBase(`/tutorial/${chapter.slug}`)} data-progress-slug={chapter.slug}>
          <div class="n">
            {String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')} · {chapter.part}
          </div>
          <div class="t">{chapter.title}</div>
          <div class="b">{chapter.blurb}</div>
          <span class="progress-mark">
            <span class="sr-only">completed</span>✓
          </span>
        </a>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <h2>Credits</h2>
  <p>
    Built on top of the official <a href="https://strudel.cc/">Strudel</a> documentation and source.
    The embedded editors are the real thing — the{' '}
    <code>@strudel/repl</code> web component. When in doubt, the{' '}
    <a href="https://strudel.cc/learn/getting-started/">official docs</a> are the source of truth.
  </p>
</Base>
